 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by a race condition in the `next()` method of `TicketSequence`, where threads could read the same value of `self._next` before acquiring a lock. The fix ensures that reading and incrementing happen atomically within a lock, preventing duplicate ticket numbers. Both the reproduction test and the full test suite now pass.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/sequence.py b/tracker/sequence.py\nindex aa19a59..d4ee246 100644\n--- a/tracker/sequence.py\n+++ b/tracker/sequence.py\n@@ -13,11 +13,10 @@ class TicketSequence:\n         self._next = value\n \n     def next(self):\n-        current = self._next\n         with self._lock:\n+            current = self._next\n             self._store(current + 1)\n         self.issued.append(current)\n         return current\n-\n     def peek(self):\n         return self._next\n",
